   506                              <1> breakRoutine:
   507                              <1> ;This subroutine is called by ^C
   508                              <1> ;Prompts the user for what they want to do.
   509                              <1> ;Preserve registers across call.
   510                              <1> ;
   511                              <1> ;We always return IRETQ which means we always execute the 
   512                              <1> ; function code that we return to DOS in eax. Unless we wish
   513                              <1> ; to terminate, we just re-attempt the function that was 
   514                              <1> ; ^C-ed.
   515                              <1> ;
